{
  "dom_id": "questionContainer",
  "name": "Question 30",
  "problem": "$6\\times \\frac{3}{8}=$",
  "worked_solution": "To multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n\\frac{6\\times 3}{8}=\\frac{18}{8}\n$$\n\nWe then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\frac{18}{8}=\\frac{18÷2}{8÷2}=\\frac{9}{4}\n$$\n\nFinally, we then convert $\\frac{9}{4}$ to a mixed number:\n\n$$\n9÷4=2\\,\\text{R}1=2\\,\\frac{1}{4}\n$$",
